From c2bd8b4c17472aab2f55cdea1ca41928f280686c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:15:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace the content of tytso-key.asc with the keyserver copy of the key
that signs releases (3AB057B7E78D945C8C5591FBD36F769BC11804F0), because
sqv cannot use the old keyring: it holds 2 v3 (PGP 2) keys, which
Sequoia does not parse, so sqv rejects the whole file (GnuPG skips such
keys silently). The other certificates in it are dropped
(52C344D60D02CD9B07031447ED3A39E393674C40,
44140F903D4FC37F4082381B475FBA0D103D4013).
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 e2fsprogs.spec |     2 +
 tytso-key.asc  | 12755 +++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 2 files changed, 5620 insertions(+), 7137 deletions(-)

diff --git a/e2fsprogs.spec b/e2fsprogs.spec
index b57180e..180c0e5 100644
--- a/e2fsprogs.spec
+++ b/e2fsprogs.spec
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@ Source1: https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/people/tytso/%{name}/v%{version
 # Also verified fingerprint matches on https://www.kernel.org/doc/wot/tytso.html
 # note that the GPG key linked off his MIT page is likely old, and is *not* the
 # same as the above key ( http://web.mit.edu/tytso/www/home.html )
+# The key(s) that sign releases, from keyservers:
+#   sq --home=none network keyserver search 3AB057B7E78D945C8C5591FBD36F769BC11804F0 --output tytso-key.asc --overwrite
 Source2: tytso-key.asc
 
 Url: http://e2fsprogs.sourceforge.net/
diff --git a/tytso-key.asc b/tytso-key.asc
